# {{PRODUCT}} Android agent instructions

Read `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; it is the authoritative safety contract.

- Anchor discovery via `task-context` / `graph`; never inspect `.agents/scripts/**` during normal app work.
- Clarify ambiguity in chat before planning. Mutations require an approved plan; after approval, execute phases autonomously. Follow-ups within active scope execute immediately: never generate redundant plan artifacts or stall for nonexistent UI buttons (`task plan-note`).
- Match chat language using the canonical cards from `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` (including the 3-section **Mobile Verification Walkthrough**). In RTL languages, start every line/option with a word in that language and wrap code/paths/English tokens in `` `backticks` ``.
- 6-tier policy (`T0_TRIVIAL` to `T5_CRITICAL`) governs gates, reviewers, and device checks. Never self-certify reviews with `record_review.py --verdict PASS`. Never poll background work. Prefer `Gemini 4 Hydrogen High` daily (on `Gemini 4 Carbon`, summarize reasoning in plain text BEFORE tool turns `#200671`), use `1–3` parallel `harness-scout-agent`s for broad discovery, implement `IMPLEMENTING` slices inline on the warm Lead session (`INLINE_LEAD_DIRECT` with concise English KDoc `/** ... */`), and never re-read subagent-analyzed files.
- Save durable rules in English via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<english-note>"` or scoped rules via `context instruct` (batch multiple rules in one call with `--entry "SCOPE :: text"`, `--batch-json`, or `--batch-file`) and follow `.agents/project-context/project-notes.md`.

## Canonical Command Catalog

| Step | Command |
|---|---|
| Discovery & Context | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` / `graph --feature <name> --json` / `context instruct "<english>" --scope <GLOBAL:*\|MODULE::name\|PACKAGE:pkg\|FEATURE:name\|PATH:rel> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" [--entry "SCOPE :: text" ...]` |
| Draft / Express | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task quick-start --outcome "..." --files <1-2-paths> --source conversation --proof-reference "<request>"` (bounded `T0`/`T1`) or `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task draft --task-id <id> --kind <AUTO\|BUG\|FEATURE\|REFACTOR\|CONFLICT> --outcome "..." --expected-files <paths> [--expected-surfaces <SURFACES>] [--phase "p1:Title" --phase "p2:Title"]` (comma-safe `--phase`, or `;` in `--phases`; `--expected-surfaces` is optional/auto-inferred: `ANALYTICS, AUTH, BILLING, BUILD_CONFIG, BUSINESS_LOGIC, COMPOSE_UI, COROUTINES, CRYPTO, DEVICE_API, DOCS, HARNESS_CONFIG, LOCALIZATION, MANIFEST_PERMISSION, NATIVE_CODE, NAVIGATION, NETWORK, PERSISTENCE, PUBLIC_API, RESOURCE_UI, ROOM_SCHEMA, SECURITY, SENSITIVE_DATA, TEST_ONLY, XML_UI`) -> `task approve --task-id <id> --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH> --source conversation --proof-reference <msg-id> --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED` |
| Gates / Ship | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task ship --task-id <id>` (or `verify-steps --task-id <id>` / `review complete-all --task <id>` / `commands [--filter <kw>]`) |
| Device / Verify | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` -> `device install-start` -> `verify --task-id <id>` |

